(* Negative control mimic-nobinding-key: mimic-key with the binding left out of the prologue (AUD-7, #425). It is the
   same model and the same attacker, the holder of the REALITY private key of the server, with bt_none on both ends: the
   first line of a stream carries no binding, and the handshake runs bound to nothing. (The code runs a stream whose line
   says "-" as an encrypted session, NOISE_SESSION_ENCRYPT, which the control leaves out: it is the binding alone that it
   takes away, as nobinding-cert does on TLS-443.) The middlebox terminates the REALITY session of alice, opens one of its
   own to bob, and the two Noise handshakes cross it unchanged, so the queries that hold in mimic-key must fail here. CI
   fails when they do not. *)

(* The selection of mimic-key, which changes only the order in which the prover resolves the rules: without it the
   prover runs without end, as on mimic-key *)
noselect a: bitstring; attacker(tpk(a)).

process
  ( Setup()
  | MimicSetup()
  | LeakRealityKey()
  | MimicSessions(bt_none, kp_on)
  )
